1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,820
Your one percent fee just ate three hundred sixteen thousand dollars.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,160
Think that sounds fake? Here's the actual math.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:12,280
You invest five hundred bucks a month for forty years. Two hundred forty grand of your money.

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:16,140
We'll assume seven percent growth a year. Not a promise, just math.

5
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:21,080
Fund A charges basically nothing. Fund B charges one percent a year.

6
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,580
That one percent is a fee the fund keeps for managing your money.

7
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,620
Tap the heart if you've never checked yours.

8
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:32,140
Ten years in, Fund B is behind by about forty-six hundred. Who really cares, right?

9
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,520
Thirty years in, it's behind by over a hundred thousand.

10
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:39,660
Send this to the friend who says one percent is nothing. Still think it's tiny?

11
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:46,460
Wait, how does that happen? The fee takes a cut of your whole pile, every single year, including the growth.

12
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:51,320
And a smaller pile? It grows slower, forever, and the gap keeps getting bigger.

13
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:54,840
Forty years in, Fund A has about one point three million.

14
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,280
Follow if this makes you want to check your account.

15
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:58,720
Fund B? About nine hundred ninety-six thousand.

16
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,900
That fee cost more than every dollar you ever put in.

17
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,180
One percent: small or not? One word.

